==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{recons|bʰergʰ-||height|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with Old Church Slavonic {{term|брѣгъ|sc=Cyrs|lang=cu}}, Proto-Germanic {{recons|bergaz|lang=gem-pro}} (English {{term|barrow|lang=en}}, German {{term|Berg|lang=de}}), Old Irish {{term|brigh||mountain|lang=sga}}, Old Armenian {{term|բարձր|sc=Armn||high|tr=barjr|lang=xcl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/'bʲerʲɪk/|lang=ru}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|lang=ru}}
{{head|ru|noun|g=m|tr=bereg}}
: N.B.— ''The irregular plural [[берега]] is actually an old dual form, since rivers have two of them.''

# [[bank]], [[shore]], [[coast]], [[beach]]
# [[land]]

